.TH git-full-merge "1" "November 2026" "SMI Toolset 0.156.0" "SMI Git Command"
.SH NAME
git-full-merge \- bring two branches up to date, merge one into the other and push, from any branch
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git full-merge
\fIFROM_BRANCH\fR \fITO_BRANCH\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
The \fBgit full-merge\fR command merges \fIFROM_BRANCH\fR into \fITO_BRANCH\fR with both branches up to
date with \fBorigin\fR, and returns to the branch it was started on with the work in progress as it was.
Each Git command is printed before it runs, as \fBExecuting: git ...\fR:
.IP 1. 4
Remembers the checked out branch. When the working tree has changes, new files included, they are put
aside with \fBgit stash push \-\-include\-untracked\fR.
.IP 2. 4
\fBgit checkout\fR \fIFROM_BRANCH\fR, \fBgit pull origin\fR \fIFROM_BRANCH\fR,
\fBgit push origin\fR \fIFROM_BRANCH\fR.
.IP 3. 4
\fBgit checkout\fR \fITO_BRANCH\fR, \fBgit pull origin\fR \fITO_BRANCH\fR,
\fBgit push origin\fR \fITO_BRANCH\fR.
.IP 4. 4
\fBgit merge \-\-no\-edit\fR \fIFROM_BRANCH\fR, then \fBgit pull origin\fR \fITO_BRANCH\fR and
\fBgit push origin\fR \fITO_BRANCH\fR.
.IP 5. 4
\fBgit checkout\fR of the branch it was started on, and \fBgit stash pop\fR when step 1 stashed.
.PP
It stops on the first failing command, for example on a merge conflict, and says on which branch it
stopped and how to get the stashed changes back:
\fBgit checkout\fR \fISTART_BRANCH\fR \fB&& git stash pop\fR. After a merge conflict, resolve the files,
\fBgit add\fR and \fBgit commit\fR them on \fITO_BRANCH\fR and push, or \fBgit merge \-\-abort\fR.
.PP
It fails at once when no branch is checked out (detached HEAD).
.PP
Git runs it as a subcommand because the executable \fBgit-full-merge\fR is in the \fBPATH\fR.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fIFROM_BRANCH\fR
The branch that is merged.
.TP
\fITO_BRANCH\fR
The branch that gets the merge and is pushed.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
On a feature branch with changes not committed yet, merge develop into master and continue:
.PP
.B git full-merge develop master
